  "nl_text": "The database schema named rschema_0195 consists of four tables: Property, Sales_Personnel, Client, and Sales_Record.\nThe Property table represents a property for sale. It has columns for Address (a string of up to 255 characters), Area (a string of up to 255 characters), Property_ID (an integer that serves as the primary key), Sale_Price (a float), and Sale_Status (a string of up to 255 characters).\nThe Sales_Personnel table represents sales personnel. It has columns for Commission_Rate (a float), Contact_Phone (an integer), Employee_ID (an integer that serves as the primary key), and Name (a string of up to 255 characters).\nThe Client table represents clients. It has columns for Address (a string of up to 255 characters), Client_ID (an integer that serves as the primary key), Contact_Phone (an integer), and Name (a string of up to 255 characters).\nThe Sales_Record table represents sales records. It has columns for Client_ID (an integer that cannot be null), Property_ID (an integer that cannot be null), Sale_Date (a datetime), Sale_Price (a float), and Sales_Personnel_ID (an integer that cannot be null). The primary key of this table is a composite of Property_ID, Employee_ID, and Client_ID. There are three foreign keys: Client_ID references the Client table, Property_ID references the Property table, and Sales_Personnel_ID references the Sales_Personnel table. The schema ensures referential integrity by enforcing the constraints on foreign keys.",
  "gold_question": "Real Estate Management System stores information on multiple properties for sale. Each property has a Property ID, address, area, sale price, and sale status. Sales personnel are identified by Employee ID, name, contact phone, and commission rate. Clients are recorded with a Client ID, name, contact phone, and address. Each sale transaction records the Property ID, sale date, sale price, sales personnel information, and client information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0195.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0195\nCREATE TABLE `property` (\n  `property_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `area` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sale_price` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sale_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`property_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_personnel` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_phone` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `commission_rate` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `client` (\n  `client_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_phone` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`client_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_record` (\n  `property_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `client_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sale_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sale_price` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`property_id`, `client_id`, `sales_personnel_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`client_id`) REFERENCES `client` (`client_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`property_id`) REFERENCES `property` (`property_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_record_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`sales_personnel_id`) REFERENCES `sales_personnel` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
